- Descriptive text that ties mustard concepts to agent behaviors\\n  - Appropriate rarity levels (mix of common to legendary)\\n  - Relevant icons (mustard/food related emojis)\\n  - Point values consistent with existing system\\n  - Trigger conditions that make sense in context\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Modifying the achievement tracking logic or database schema\\n- Changing the UI components for displaying achievements\\n- Adding achievements in other categories\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n**R1: Category Addition**\\n- Add `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS = \\"famous_mustards\\"` to the AchievementCategory enum\\n\\n**R2: Achievement Definitions**\\n- Create exactly 10 new Achievement objects\\n- Each must reference famous mustard varieties (Dijon, Yellow, Honey Mustard, Spicy Brown, etc.)\\n- Names should be creative but clearly mustard-themed\\n- Descriptions should cleverly relate mustard characteristics to agent behaviors\\n- Must follow existing achievement patterns and structure\\n\\n**R3: Quality Standards**\\n- Achievements should have varied rarity levels (suggested: 3-4 common, 3-4 uncommon, 2-3 rare, 0-1 epic/legendary)\\n- Point values should align with rarity (10-15 common, 20-35 uncommon, 40-60 rare, 75+ epic/legendary)\\n- Icons should be food/mustard related emojis\\n- Trigger conditions should be realistic and achievable\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n\\n**T1: Code Integration**\\n- Achievements must be added to the existing ACHIEVEMENTS list in achievements.py\\n- Follow existing code structure and formatting\\n- No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n\\n**T2: Naming Conventions**\\n- Achievement IDs should follow snake_case pattern\\n- IDs should be descriptive and mustard-themed\\n- Names should be title case and engaging\\n\\n### Constraints\\n\\n**C1: System Compatibility**\\n- Must work with existing achievement tracking system\\n- Cannot modify database schema or core tracking logic\\n- Must use existing trigger condition patterns\\n\\n**C2: Theme Consistency**\\n- All achievements must be mustard-themed\\n- Should maintain the humorous, gaming-style tone of existing achievements\\n- Must fit naturally with the existing achievement ecosystem\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. \\u2705 10 new achievements added to the system\\n2. \\u2705 All achievements are mustard-themed and creative\\n3. \\u2705 Code integrates cleanly without breaking existing functionality\\n4. \\u2705 Achievements follow established patterns for structure and quality\\n5. \\u2705 Mixed rarity distribution provides progression incentives\\n6. \\u2705 Trigger conditions are realistic and varied\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- The existing achievement system architecture will not change\\n- The mustard theme should be applied broadly (types, brands, characteristics, uses)\\n- Achievements should maintain the existing humorous and gaming-inspired tone\\n- Standard software development practices will be followed\\n\\n## Technical Context\\n\\nThe system already has these achievement categories:\\n- SKA, BRASS_BAND, DRUM_CORPS, GUITAR_HERO (music-themed)\\n- PRODUCTIVITY, COMEDY, MILESTONE, STREAK, META (behavior-themed)\\n\\nThe new FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category will join this list and achievements will be added to the main ACHIEVEMENTS list in `/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MbCH7hB82aasAD6fvT6Etp', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Fidget Spinner Achievements - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nAdd 10 new achievements from the "famous mustards" category to the existing achievement system in the ensemble project. This is a focused code enhancement that builds upon existing infrastructure without requiring UI or database changes.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Foundation Setup (Phase 1)\n**Objective**: Establish the new FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category and prepare the codebase\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Add FAMOUS_MUSTARDS enum value to AchievementCategory\n- Research famous mustard varieties for achievement themes\n- Validate existing achievement system structure\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category added to enum without breaking existing code\n- Code compiles and runs without errors\n- All existing achievements remain functional\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Estimated Duration**: 1 development cycle\n\n### Milestone 2: Achievement Design & Implementation (Phase 2) \n**Objective**: Create and implement all 10 mustard-themed achievements\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- 10 new Achievement objects with mustard themes\n- Varied rarity distribution (3-4 common, 3-4 uncommon, 2-3 rare, 0-1 epic/legendary)\n- Creative names and descriptions linking mustard characteristics to agent behaviors\n- Appropriate point values and trigger conditions\n- Mustard/food-related emoji icons\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All 10 achievements added to ACHIEVEMENTS list\n- Each achievement follows existing structure and patterns\n- Rarity and point values align with existing system standards\n- Trigger conditions are realistic and achievable\n- All achievements compile and integrate without errors\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\n**Estimated Duration**: 2 development cycles\n\n### Milestone 3: Testing & Quality Assurance (Phase 3)\n**Objective**: Verify system functionality and achievement quality\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Comprehensive test coverage for new achievements\n- Integration testing with existing achievement system\n- Code review and quality validation\n- Documentation updates if needed\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All tests pass without errors\n- New achievements trigger correctly in system\n- No regression issues with existing functionality\n- Code follows project standards and conventions\n- Achievement themes are creative and engaging\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 complete\n**Estimated Duration**: 1 development cycle\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n**Low Risk Items**:\n- Category enum addition (simple, non-breaking change)\n- Achievement object creation (follows established patterns)\n\n**Medium Risk Items**:\n- Theme creativity and quality (subjective, requires review)\n- Trigger condition realism (needs testing)\n\n**Mitigation Strategies**:\n- Follow existing achievement patterns closely\n- Test trigger conditions thoroughly\n- Review achievement themes for quality and humor\n\n## Resource Requirements\n\n**Technical Skills Needed**:\n- Python development\n- Understanding of existing achievement system\n- Test development and execution\n\n**Key Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py` (primary modification)\n- Test files for achievement system\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n1. **Functionality**: All 10 achievements integrate without breaking existing system\n2. **Quality**: Achievements are creative, humorous, and thematically consistent\n3. **Standards**: Code follows project conventions and passes all tests\n4. **Integration**: New category works seamlessly with existing achievement tracking\n\n## Final Deliverables\n\nUpon project completion:\n- 10 new FAMOUS_MUSTARDS achievements in production system\n- Updated achievement category enum\n- Comprehensive test coverage\n- Clean, maintainable code following project standards'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MbCH7hB82aasAD6fvT6Etp', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_030238.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_030238.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MzZgNbveNNxyTwFmFvpoxn', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Fidget Spinner Achievements'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MzZgNbveNNxyTwFmFvpoxn', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013Z1gnUE9iY8MfHNo4Xp7FH', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Fidget Spinner Achievements'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013Z1gnUE9iY8MfHNo4Xp7FH', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal for Famous Mustards achievement system integration - minimal-risk extension approach leveraging existing data-driven patterns", "key_decisions": ["Extension Pattern: Pure data addition to existing ACHIEVEMENTS list with zero logic changes", "Tech Stack: Maintain existing Python/dataclass/enum architecture - no new technologies needed", "Integration Strategy: Add FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category and 10 achievements to current achievements.py file", "Risk Mitigation: Single-file modification approach minimizes breaking change potential", "Testing Strategy: Leverage existing achievement evaluation engine with mustard-specific integration tests"], "self_analysis": "Successfully analyzed the existing achievement system architecture and designed a minimal-risk extension approach. The proposal balances creative mustard theming with technical pragmatism, using established patterns to ensure seamless integration. The comprehensive analysis covers all technical aspects while maintaining focus on the core requirement of adding 10 mustard-themed achievements."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017hvPxQrVGG9hBVMQ7ofv6B', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017hvPxQrVGG9hBVMQ7ofv6B', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Famous Mustards Achievements - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### High-Level System Design\\nThis is a **pure feature addition** to an existing achievement system. The architecture follows the **extension pattern** - minimal changes to existing code while adding new functionality that seamlessly integrates with established patterns.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Data-driven configuration with enumerated categories\\n- New achievement definitions are added to the existing `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\\n- Category enumeration is extended with `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS`\\n- Zero modifications to tracking logic, UI, or database schema\\n- Leverages existing trigger condition patterns and evaluation engine\\n\\n### Design Philosophy\\n**\\"Mustard never goes out of style\\"** - Just like the condiment shelf staple, these achievements should feel natural and enduring within the existing system, maintaining the humorous tone while adding thematic variety.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Language & Framework\\n- **Python 3.8+** (matches existing codebase)\\n- **SQLite** (existing achievement tracking database)\\n- **Dataclasses & Enums** (existing architecture pattern)\\n\\n**Rationale**: The existing system is well-architected with Python dataclasses and enums. No compelling reason to introduce new technologies for a simple feature addition. The existing `Achievement` and `AchievementCategory` classes provide all needed functionality.\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered**:\\n- JSON configuration files: Rejected - would break type safety and IDE support\\n- Separate database table: Rejected - unnecessary complexity for simple category addition\\n- Plugin system: Rejected - over-engineering for this scope\\n\\n---\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Component Breakdown\\n\\n#### 1. **Achievement Category Extension**\\n**File**: `src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`\\n**Responsibility**: Add new enum value to existing `AchievementCategory`\\n**Change**: Single line addition: `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS = \\"famous_mustards\\"`\\n\\n#### 2. **Achievement Definitions**\\n**Responsibility**: 10 new `Achievement` objects with mustard themes\\n**Integration**: Added to existing `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\\n**Structure**: Each achievement follows existing pattern with mustard-specific:\\n- IDs (snake_case, mustard-themed)\\n- Names (creative mustard references)\\n- Descriptions (mustard characteristics \\u2192 agent behaviors)\\n- Categories (all `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS`)\\n- Appropriate rarity distribution and points\\n\\n#### 3. **Existing System Integration Points**\\n**Achievement Tracker**: No changes needed - automatically processes new achievements\\n**Database Schema**: No changes needed - achievements are stored by string ID\\n**UI Display**: No changes needed - category enum automatically appears\\n**Trigger Engine**: No changes needed - uses existing condition patterns\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nAgent Execution \\u2192 AchievementTracker.check_and_award() \\n    \\u2192 Iterates through ALL achievements in ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n    \\u2192 Evaluates trigger_condition for each (including new mustard ones)\\n    \\u2192 Awards matching achievements\\n    \\u2192 Stores in SQLite with achievement_id reference\\n```\\n\\n**Key Point**: New achievements automatically participate in the existing evaluation loop with zero logic changes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/agents/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 achievements.py                 # MODIFIED - Only file that changes\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementCategory enum   # ADD: FAMOUS_MUSTARDS value\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ACHIEVEMENTS list          # ADD: 10 new Achievement objects\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 [all other files unchanged]\\n```\\n\\n**Proposed Achievement Organization Within File**:\\n```python\\n# Existing achievements remain unchanged\\n\\n# ===== FAMOUS MUSTARDS ACHIEVEMENTS =====\\n# (New section added to ACHIEVEMENTS list)\\nAchievement(id=\\"dijon_sophistication\\", ...),\\nAchievement(id=\\"yellow_classic\\", ...),\\nAchievement(id=\\"honey_sweetness\\", ...),\\n# ... 7 more\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Achievement Structure (Existing, Unchanged)\\n```python\\n@dataclass\\nclass Achievement:\\n    id: str                    # e.g. \\"dijon_sophistication\\"\\n    name: str                  # e.g. \\"Dijon Sophistication\\"\\n    description: str           # Mustard trait \\u2192 agent behavior\\n    category: AchievementCategory  # FAMOUS_MUSTARDS\\n    rarity: AchievementRarity     # COMMON, UNCOMMON, RARE, EPIC, LEGENDARY\\n    icon: str                     # Food/mustard emojis\\n    points: int                   # 10-15 common, 75+ legendary\\n    agent_classes: List[str]      # [\\"*\\"] for all, or specific classes\\n    trigger_condition: Dict       # When to award\\n```\\n\\n### Proposed Achievements Schema\\n| ID | Name | Rarity | Points | Theme |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| dijon_sophistication | Dijon Sophistication | UNCOMMON | 25 | Premium mustard \\u2192 elegant solution |\\n| yellow_classic | Yellow Classic | COMMON | 15 | Basic mustard \\u2192 foundational work |\\n| honey_sweetness | Honey Mustard Sweetness | UNCOMMON | 30 | Sweet mustard \\u2192 user-friendly output |\\n| spicy_brown_heat | Spicy Brown Heat | RARE | 45 | Spicy mustard \\u2192 handling pressure |\\n| english_tradition | English Mustard Tradition | RARE | 50 | Traditional strong mustard \\u2192 reliability |\\n| beer_mustard_craft | Beer Mustard Craftsman | EPIC | 75 | Craft mustard \\u2192 artisanal code |\\n| whole_grain_texture | Whole Grain Texture | UNCOMMON | 30 | Textured mustard \\u2192 rich detail |\\n| chinese_hot_fire | Chinese Hot Mustard Fire | LEGENDARY | 100 | Hottest mustard \\u2192 extreme performance |\\n| wasabi_fusion | Wasabi Fusion | RARE | 55 | Fusion mustard \\u2192 cross-platform work |\\n| stadium_classic | Stadium Mustard | COMMON | 20 | Ballpark mustard \\u2192 team collaboration |\\n\\n### Database Integration (Existing Schema, Unchanged)\\n- `awarded_achievements` table stores achievements by `achievement_id` string\\n- No schema changes needed - mustard achievement IDs work with existing structure\\n- Achievement metadata lives in Python code, not database\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Trigger Condition Design\\n\\n### Existing Trigger Patterns (Leveraged)\\n```python\\n# Event-based\\n{\\"event\\": \\"elegant_solution\\"}\\n\\n# Metric-based  \\n{\\"successful_executions\\": {\\"min\\": 10}}\\n\\n# Time-based\\n{\\"duration_ms\\": {\\"min\\": 600000}}\\n\\n# Combination conditions\\n{\\"event\\": \\"cross_stack_collaboration\\", \\"success\\": True}\\n```\\n\\n### Proposed Mustard-Specific Conditions\\n```python\\n# Sophistication (Dijon) - elegant, efficient solutions\\n{\\"iterations\\": {\\"max\\": 2}, \\"success\\": True}\\n\\n# Classic reliability (Yellow) - steady performance \\n{\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": 5}}\\n\\n# Sweet user experience (Honey Mustard)\\n{\\"event\\": \\"user_friendly_output\\"}\\n\\n# Heat under pressure (Spicy Brown)\\n{\\"event\\": \\"high_pressure_success\\"}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing Approach\\n**File**: `tests/test_mustard_achievements.py` (new)\\n**Focus**: Verify achievement definitions are valid\\n```python\\ndef test_mustard_category_exists()\\ndef test_mustard_achievements_structure()\\ndef test_mustard_rarity_distribution() \\ndef test_mustard_trigger_conditions()\\n```\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n**Existing tests should pass unchanged** - validates backward compatibility\\n**Add mustard-specific integration tests**:\\n```python\\ndef test_mustard_achievements_awarded()\\ndef test_mustard_achievements_in_database()\\n```\\n\\n### Manual Verification\\n1. Run existing achievement system\\n2. Trigger conditions that should award mustard achievements\\n3. Verify achievements appear in UI with correct metadata\\n4. Confirm database entries are created correctly\\n\\n### Quality Assurance Checklist\\n- [ ] 10 achievements with unique IDs\\n- [ ] All reference mustard varieties/characteristics  \\n- [ ] Rarity distribution: 3 common, 4 uncommon, 2 rare, 1 epic/legendary\\n- [ ] Points align with rarity levels\\n- [ ] Creative names and descriptions maintain humor\\n- [ ] Trigger conditions are realistic and varied\\n- [ ] All achievements use `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS` category\\n- [ ] Food/mustard emoji icons selected\\n- [ ] No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Environment\\n1. **Backup current achievements.py** (safety first)\\n2. **Add FAMOUS_MUSTARDS** to `AchievementCategory` enum\\n3. **Add 10 mustard achievements** to `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\\n4. **Test locally** using existing test suite + new tests\\n\\n### Code Review Checklist\\n- [ ] Code follows existing patterns exactly\\n- [ ] Achievement IDs are unique (no conflicts)\\n- [ ] Trigger conditions use established patterns\\n- [ ] Rarity distribution is appropriate\\n- [ ] Points values are consistent with existing system\\n- [ ] All mustard achievements use correct category\\n- [ ] No modifications to core tracking logic\\n- [ ] Backward compatibility maintained\\n\\n### Production Deployment\\n**Zero downtime deployment** - achievements are loaded from Python code at startup\\n1. Deploy updated `achievements.py`\\n2. Restart application (picks up new achievements)\\n3. Verify new category appears in UI\\n4. Monitor for achievement awards\\n\\n### Rollback Plan\\nSimple file replacement - revert `achievements.py` to previous version if issues arise.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Separate Configuration File\\n**Approach**: JSON/YAML file for mustard achievements\\n**Pros**: Could be modified without code changes\\n**Cons**: \\n- Breaks type safety (no IDE support for Achievement fields)\\n- Requires new loading logic\\n- Creates second source of truth\\n- Over-engineering for 10 static definitions\\n**Verdict**: Rejected - existing pattern works well\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Database-Driven Achievements\\n**Approach**: Store achievement definitions in database tables\\n**Pros**: Dynamic achievement management\\n**Cons**:\\n- Major architectural change outside scope\\n- Would require database migrations \\n- Much higher complexity\\n- Performance overhead for static data\\n**Verdict**: Rejected - scope creep\\n\\n### Alternative 3: Plugin/Extension System\\n**Approach**: Achievement modules as plugins\\n**Pros**: Theoretical extensibility\\n**Cons**:\\n- Massive over-engineering for simple addition\\n- Would require new plugin architecture\\n- Adds complexity without clear benefit\\n**Verdict**: Rejected - YAGNI principle\\n\\n### Alternative 4: Separate Mustard Category File\\n**Approach**: Import mustard achievements from separate module\\n**Pros**: Code organization\\n**Cons**:\\n- Breaks established pattern (all achievements in one file)\\n- More complex imports\\n- Doesn\'t provide meaningful benefit\\n**Verdict**: Rejected -