{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 03:05:56", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-cbc2a307-060d-43d1-9cb7-7191ce32ab58', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Implement Milestone 1: Backend File Tracking Infrastructure with efficient file change tracking system, API endpoints for file change detection, optimized metadata caching, and bulk status checking to replace unreliable file update mechanism",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "backend_tasks_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md",\n  "test_tasks_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Dzp6ZJ3LF8ReYY3GhVAgJ4', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Dzp6ZJ3LF8ReYY3GhVAgJ4', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Famous Mustards Achievements - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nAdd 10 new achievements from the category \\"famous mustards\\" to the existing achievement system in the ensemble project.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a new achievement category `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS` in the existing system\\n2. Design 10 thematic achievements based on famous mustard varieties and mustard-related concepts\\n3. Integrate these achievements into the existing achievement tracking system\\n4. Ensure achievements follow the established pattern and quality standards\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Add `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS` to the `AchievementCategory` enum\\n- Create 10 new achievement definitions with:\\n  - Unique IDs related to mustard themes\\n  - Creative names referencing famous mustard types/brands\\n  - Descriptive text that ties mustard concepts to agent behaviors\\n  - Appropriate rarity levels (mix of common to legendary)\\n  - Relevant icons (mustard/food related emojis)\\n  - Point values consistent with existing system\\n  - Trigger conditions that make sense in context\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Modifying the achievement tracking logic or database schema\\n- Changing the UI components for displaying achievements\\n- Adding achievements in other categories\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n**R1: Category Addition**\\n- Add `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS = \\"famous_mustards\\"` to the AchievementCategory enum\\n\\n**R2: Achievement Definitions**\\n- Create exactly 10 new Achievement objects\\n- Each must reference famous mustard varieties (Dijon, Yellow, Honey Mustard, Spicy Brown, etc.)\\n- Names should be creative but clearly mustard-themed\\n- Descriptions should cleverly relate mustard characteristics to agent behaviors\\n- Must follow existing achievement patterns and structure\\n\\n**R3: Quality Standards**\\n- Achievements should have varied rarity levels (suggested: 3-4 common, 3-4 uncommon, 2-3 rare, 0-1 epic/legendary)\\n- Point values should align with rarity (10-15 common, 20-35 uncommon, 40-60 rare, 75+ epic/legendary)\\n- Icons should be food/mustard related emojis\\n- Trigger conditions should be realistic and achievable\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n\\n**T1: Code Integration**\\n- Achievements must be added to the existing ACHIEVEMENTS list in achievements.py\\n- Follow existing code structure and formatting\\n- No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n\\n**T2: Naming Conventions**\\n- Achievement IDs should follow snake_case pattern\\n- IDs should be descriptive and mustard-themed\\n- Names should be title case and engaging\\n\\n### Constraints\\n\\n**C1: System Compatibility**\\n- Must work with existing achievement tracking system\\n- Cannot modify database schema or core tracking logic\\n- Must use existing trigger condition patterns\\n\\n**C2: Theme Consistency**\\n- All achievements must be mustard-themed\\n- Should maintain the humorous, gaming-style tone of existing achievements\\n- Must fit naturally with the existing achievement ecosystem\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. \\u2705 10 new achievements added to the system\\n2. \\u2705 All achievements are mustard-themed and creative\\n3. \\u2705 Code integrates cleanly without breaking existing functionality\\n4. \\u2705 Achievements follow established patterns for structure and quality\\n5. \\u2705 Mixed rarity distribution provides progression incentives\\n6. \\u2705 Trigger conditions are realistic and varied\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- The existing achievement system architecture will not change\\n- The mustard theme should be applied broadly (types, brands, characteristics, uses)\\n- Achievements should maintain the existing humorous and gaming-inspired tone\\n- Standard software development practices will be followed\\n\\n## Technical Context\\n\\nThe system already has these achievement categories:\\n- SKA, BRASS_BAND, DRUM_CORPS, GUITAR_HERO (music-themed)\\n- PRODUCTIVITY, COMEDY, MILESTONE, STREAK, META (behavior-themed)\\n\\nThe new FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category will join this list and achievements will be added to the main ACHIEVEMENTS list in `/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DuwyKFk4knrMJwxuXneTMC', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DuwyKFk4knrMJwxuXneTMC', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# File Pane Stability Improvement - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### High-Level System Design\\nThe architecture implements a **Intelligent Polling Pattern** with backend file change tracking to replace unreliable WebSocket or basic polling mechanisms. This hybrid approach provides real-time updates while maintaining connection stability and reducing overhead.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n**Event-Driven Polling with State Synchronization**\\n- Backend maintains file change state with timestamps and checksums\\n- Frontend implements adaptive polling with exponential backoff\\n- Optimized API endpoints minimize payload and processing overhead\\n- Client-side state management ensures UI consistency\\n\\n### Rationale\\nThis approach balances real-time responsiveness with reliability. Unlike WebSockets (which can drop connections) or naive polling (which wastes resources), this design provides predictable behavior while adapting to system load and network conditions.\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **React** (assumed existing): Component-based UI with efficient re-rendering\\n- **Redux Toolkit**: State management for file list and update tracking\\n- **RTK Query**: Efficient data fetching with automatic caching and synchronization\\n- **React.useMemo/useCallback**: Performance optimization for frequent updates\\n\\n*Why React/Redux?* Provides predictable state updates crucial for file list consistency. RTK Query\'s automatic caching prevents unnecessary API calls.\\n\\n*Alternative considered:* Pure React hooks + Context API. Rejected due to complexity of managing polling state and cache invalidation.\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Node.js/Express** (assumed existing): RESTful API with file system monitoring\\n- **chokidar**: Efficient file system watching across platforms\\n- **Redis**: Optional caching layer for file metadata and change tracking\\n- **fs.promises**: Async file system operations\\n\\n*Why Node.js?* Native file system integration and event-driven architecture align perfectly with file monitoring requirements.\\n\\n*Alternative considered:* Polling-only approach without file watching. Rejected due to higher resource usage and potential delays.\\n\\n### API Design\\n- **REST**: Stateless, cacheable, simple to debug\\n- **JSON**: Lightweight payload format\\n- **ETags**: HTTP-based caching and change detection\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n\\n#### FileListContainer\\n- **Responsibility**: Manages polling lifecycle and file list state\\n- **Interactions**: Dispatches RTK Query hooks, manages polling intervals\\n- **State**: Current file list, last update timestamp, polling status\\n\\n#### FileListDisplay\\n- **Responsibility**: Pure presentation of file list\\n- **Interactions**: Receives file data from container, handles user actions\\n- **Optimizations**: React.memo to prevent unnecessary re-renders\\n\\n#### FilePollingService\\n- **Responsibility**: Adaptive polling logic with exponential backoff\\n- **Interactions**: Calls API endpoints, manages timing strategies\\n- **Features**: Network error handling, automatic retry logic\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n\\n#### FileWatcher\\n```\\nFileWatcher\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 monitors file system changes (chokidar)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 maintains change timestamps\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 calculates file checksums for integrity\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 triggers cache invalidation\\n```\\n\\n#### FileListAPI\\n```\\nFileListAPI\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 GET /api/files/list?since=timestamp\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 GET /api/files/changes?etag=value\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 provides optimized file metadata\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 handles conditional requests (304 Not Modified)\\n```\\n\\n#### ChangeTracker\\n```\\nChangeTracker\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 stores file change events\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 maintains ETag/timestamp mappings\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 provides incremental update data\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 cleans up old change records\\n```\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow\\n\\n```\\n[File System] -> [FileWatcher] -> [ChangeTracker] -> [Redis Cache]\\n                                                          |\\n[FileListDisplay] <- [FileListContainer] <- [FilePollingService] <- [FileListAPI]\\n```\\n\\n### Update Sequence\\n1. User action or file system change occurs\\n2. FileWatcher detects change and updates ChangeTracker\\n3. ChangeTracker invalidates relevant cache entries\\n4. FilePollingService makes conditional API request\\n5. API returns changed files or 304 Not Modified\\n6. FileListContainer updates Redux state\\n7. FileListDisplay re-renders with new data\\n\\n## 5. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileList/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileListContainer.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileListDisplay.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileListItem.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 common/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 filePollingService.js\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 fileAPI.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 errorHandling.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 store/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 slices/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileListSlice.js\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileListAPI.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useFilePolling.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useFileList.js\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 pollingStrategies.js\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileHelpers.js\\n\\nbackend/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routes/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 files.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileWatcher.js\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ChangeTracker.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 FileSystemService.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 middleware/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 caching.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 etag.js\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileHelpers.js\\n```\\n\\n## 6. Data Model\\n\\n### Frontend State (Redux)\\n```typescript\\ninterface FileListState {\\n  files: FileItem[]\\n  lastUpdated: timestamp\\n  pollingStatus: \'idle\' | \'polling\' | \'error\'\\n  errorMessage: string | null\\n}\\n\\ninterface FileItem {\\n  id: string\\n  name: string\\n  path: string\\n  modifiedAt: timestamp\\n  size: number\\n  type: \'file\' | \'directory\'\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Backend Data Structures\\n```typescript\\ninterface FileChange {\\n  id: string\\n  timestamp: number\\n  type: \'created\' | \'modified\' | \'deleted\'\\n  file: FileMetadata\\n}\\n\\ninterface FileMetadata {\\n  path: string\\n  name: string\\n  size: number\\n  modifiedAt: number\\n  checksum: string\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 7. API Design\\n\\n### Endpoints\\n\\n#### GET /api/files/list\\n**Purpose**: Retrieve current file list with optional filtering\\n```\\nQuery Parameters:\\n- since: timestamp (optional) - only files changed after this time\\n- etag: string (optional) - for conditional requests\\n\\nResponse:\\n{\\n  \\"files\\": FileItem[],\\n  \\"timestamp\\": number,\\n  \\"etag\\": string\\n}\\n\\nStatus Codes:\\n- 200: Success with data\\n- 304: Not Modified (when using etag)\\n- 500: Server error\\n```\\n\\n#### GET /api/files/changes\\n**Purpose**: Get incremental changes since last request\\n```\\nQuery Parameters:\\n- since: timestamp (required) - last known timestamp\\n- etag: string (optional) - for cache validation\\n\\nResponse:\\n{\\n  \\"changes\\": FileChange[],\\n  \\"timestamp\\": number,\\n  \\"etag\\": string,\\n  \\"hasMore\\": boolean\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Authentication\\nAssumes existing authentication middleware is in place. All endpoints should require valid session/token.\\n\\n## 8. Polling Strategy\\n\\n### Adaptive Polling Algorithm\\n```javascript\\n// Base intervals in milliseconds\\nconst INTERVALS = {\\n  ACTIVE: 1000,      // When recent changes detected\\n  NORMAL: 5000,      // Regular polling\\n  IDLE: 15000,       // When no changes for extended time\\n  ERROR: 30000       // After errors (with exponential backoff)\\n}\\n\\n// Backoff strategy\\nfunction calculateDelay(errorCount) {\\n  return Math.min(INTERVALS.ERROR * Math.pow(2, errorCount), 300000) // Max 5 min\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Polling State Machine\\n1. **Active**: Recent file changes detected, poll every 1s\\n2. **Normal**: No recent changes, poll every 5s\\n3. **Idle**: No changes for 5+ minutes, poll every 15s\\n4. **Error**: Network/server issues, exponential backoff\\n\\n## 9. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n```javascript\\n// config/polling.js\\nmodule.exports = {\\n  development: {\\n    pollingInterval: 2000,\\n    fileWatchDebounce: 100,\\n    cacheEnabled: false\\n  },\\n  production: {\\n    pollingInterval: 5000,\\n    fileWatchDebounce: 300,\\n    cacheEnabled: true,\\n    redisUrl: process.env.REDIS_URL\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### CI/CD Considerations\\n- **Feature Flags**: Gradual rollout of new polling mechanism\\n- **Monitoring**: Track polling frequency, error rates, cache hit ratios\\n- **Rollback Plan**: Ability to revert to previous file update mechanism\\n\\n### Docker Configuration\\n```dockerfile\\n# Add to existing Dockerfile\\nCOPY src/services/filePolling* ./src/services/\\nCOPY backend/services/File* ./backend/services/\\nENV POLLING_STRATEGY=adaptive\\nENV FILE_WATCH_ENABLED=true\\n```\\n\\n## 10. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n**Frontend**:\\n- FilePollingService logic and timing\\n- Redux slice reducers and actions\\n- Component rendering with different file states\\n\\n**Backend**:\\n- FileWatcher event handling\\n- ChangeTracker data integrity\\n- API endpoint responses and caching\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- End-to-end file change propagation\\n- Polling behavior under various network conditions\\n- Cache invalidation scenarios\\n- Error recovery and backoff strategies\\n\\n### Performance Testing\\n- Polling frequency under high file change volumes\\n- Memory usage with large file lists\\n- API response times with incremental updates\\n\\n### Test Files Structure\\n```\\ntests/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 unit/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 filePollingService.test.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 fileListSlice.test.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileWatcher.test.js\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ChangeTracker.test.js\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileAPI.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 integration/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 fileUpdateFlow.test.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 pollingBehavior.test.js\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 performance/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 pollingLoad.test.js\\n```\\n\\n## 11. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### WebSocket Approach\\n**Pros**: True real-time updates, minimal client logic\\n**Cons**: Connection reliability issues, more complex error handling\\n**Verdict**: Rejected due to explicit constraint against WebSockets\\n\\n### Server-Sent Events (SSE)\\n**Pros**: Simpler than WebSockets, automatic reconnection\\n**Cons**: Limited browser support, connection overhead\\n**Verdict**: Considered but polling provides better control over update frequency\\n\\n### Basic Polling\\n**Pros**: Simple implementation, predictable behavior\\n**Cons**: Inefficient network usage, fixed update intervals\\n**Verdict**: Enhanced with intelligent/adaptive polling for better performance\\n\\n### File System Notifications + Long Polling\\n**Pros**: Immediate updates, efficient for sparse changes\\n**Cons**: Complex state management, potential timeout issues\\n**Verdict**: Complexity outweighs benefits for this use case\\n\\n## 12. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk: Polling Overhead\\n**Mitigation**: Adaptive intervals, conditional requests (ETags), efficient payloads\\n\\n### Risk: Cache Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**: Checksum-based integrity checking, atomic cache updates\\n\\n### Risk: Network Interruption\\n**Mitigation**: Exponential backoff, automatic retry logic, graceful degradation\\n\\n### Risk: File System Overload\\n**Mitigation**: Debounced file watching, batched change notifications\\n\\n### Risk: Memory Leaks\\n**Mitigation**: Cleanup polling timers on unmount, bounded cache sizes\\n\\n## 13. Open Questions\\n\\n### User Preferences Needed:\\n1. **Polling Frequency**: Balance between responsiveness and resource usage\\n   - Conservative (5-15s intervals) vs Aggressive (1-3s intervals)\\n\\n2. **Error Recovery**: How aggressively to retry after errors\\n   - Quick recovery vs Patient backoff\\n\\n3. **Cache Strategy**: Local storage vs memory-only for file state\\n   - Persistence across page refreshes vs Simplified state management\\n\\n4. **Update Granularity**: Full file list vs incremental changes\\n   - Simpler implementation vs Network efficiency\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input:\\n- Should we persist polling state across browser sessions?\\n- What level of file change detail should be exposed to UI?\\n- Should polling pause when tab is not visible?\\n\\n## 14. Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Frontend Optimization\\n- **React.memo**: Prevent unnecessary component re-renders\\n- **Virtualization**: For large file lists (1000+ files)\\n- **Debounced Filtering**: Smooth search/filter interactions\\n- **Background Tab Handling**: Reduce polling when tab inactive\\n\\n### Backend Optimization\\n- **Change Batching**: Group multiple file changes in single API response\\n- **Compression**: Gzip API responses for large file lists\\n- **Index Optimization**: Fast file lookups by path/timestamp\\n- **Connection Pooling**: Efficient database connections for change tracking\\n\\n## 15. Monitoring and Observability\\n\\n### Metrics to Track\\n- Average polling interval\\n- API response times\\n- Cache hit/miss ratios\\n- File change detection latency\\n- Error rates by type\\n\\n### Logging Strategy\\n```javascript\\n// Example logging points\\nlogger.info(\'Polling cycle started\', { interval, timestamp })\\nlogger.warn(\'Network error during polling\', { error, retryCount })\\nlogger.debug(\'File changes detected\', { fileCount, changes })\\n```\\n\\n### Alerts\\n- High error rates in polling\\n- Unusual file change volumes\\n- API performance degradation\\n- Cache invalidation failures\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, maintainable solution for file pane stability while meeting all specified constraints and success criteria."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NorBiULLMNSnTzHCSnpqeK', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NorBiULLMNSnTzHCSnpqeK', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Backend Tasks - AchievementToast Component Enhancement\\n\\n## Task 1: Achievement Metadata Update\\n- **Name**: Extend Achievement Data Model\\n- **Description**: Add agent name retrieval support to achievement metadata\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Update Achievement data model to include optional agent name field\\n  * Ensure backward compatibility with existing achievements\\n  * Create data access method to retrieve agent name from achievement record\\n- **Complexity**: Simple\\n- **Dependencies**: None\\n\\n## Task 2: Achievement Retrieval Service Enhancement\\n- **Name**: Update Achievement Retrieval Service\\n- **Description**: Modify backend service to include agent name when fetching achievements\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Update API response to optionally include agent name data\\n  * Create new query method supporting agent name retrieval\\n  * Add type-safe serialization for new data field\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Metadata Update)\\n\\n## Task 3: API Endpoint Modification\\n- **Name**: Update Achievement API Endpoints\\n- **Description**: Extend REST API to support agent name in achievement responses\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Modify `/achievements` and `/achievements/{id}` endpoints\\n  * Add optional `include_agent_name` query parameter\\n  * Implement conditional agent name inclusion\\n  * Update OpenAPI/Swagger documentation\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 2 (Achievement Retrieval Service)\\n\\n## Task 4: Error Handling and Validation\\n- **Name**: Implement Robust Error Handling\\n- **Description**: Add comprehensive error handling for agent name retrieval\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Handle cases where agent name is not available\\n  * Create specific error responses for missing agent data\\n  * Log any agent name retrieval issues\\n  * Ensure no performance impact when agent name is not needed\\n- **Complexity**: Simple\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 3 (API Endpoint Modification)\\n\\n## Task 5: Performance Optimization\\n- **Name**: Optimize Agent Name Retrieval\\n- **Description**: Implement efficient caching and retrieval for agent names\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Add in-memory caching for frequently accessed agent names\\n  * Create cache invalidation strategy\\n  * Minimize additional database queries\\n  * Implement configurable cache timeout\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 4 (Error Handling)\\n\\n## Dependency Graph\\n```\\nTask 1 (Metadata Update)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Task 2 (Retrieval Service)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Task 3 (API Endpoints)\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Task 4 (Error Handling)\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Task 5 (Performance Optimization)\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Use existing authentication and authorization mechanisms\\n- Maintain JSON structure compatibility\\n- Minimize performance overhead\\n- Follow existing error handling patterns\\n\\n## Estimated Effort\\n- Total estimated development time: 2-3 days\\n- Complexity: Medium\\n- Recommended team: 1-2 backend developers\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n- Risk: Performance degradation\\n  Mitigation: Implement intelligent caching, lazy loading\\n- Risk: Backward compatibility issues\\n  Mitigation: Careful API design, optional fields, feature flags\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n- How should missing agent names be represented?\\n- What is the expected frequency of agent name retrieval?\\n- Are there any privacy considerations for agent name exposure?"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FFM9ritDKT3J64PVVKkrZL', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FFM9ritDKT3J64PVVKkrZL', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Test Strategy: Backend File Tracking and Intelligent Polling\\n\\n## Test Coverage Overview\\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 80%\\n- **Integration Test Coverage**: 90%\\n- **E2E Test Coverage**: Critical user flows\\n\\n## Backend Test Tasks\\n\\n### FileWatcher Service Tests\\n1. **Unit Tests**:\\n   - Verify file system change detection\\n   - Test checksum generation accuracy\\n   - Validate timestamp tracking\\n   - Handle edge cases (file rename, permission changes)\\n\\n2. **Integration Tests**:\\n   - Verify file change events propagation\\n   - Test interaction with ChangeTracker\\n   - Validate cache invalidation triggers\\n   - Performance testing with large file sets\\n\\n### ChangeTracker Service Tests\\n1. **Unit Tests**:\\n   - Test change event storage\\n   - Validate ETag generation\\n   - Check timestamp-based filtering\\n   - Verify cleanup of old change records\\n\\n2. **Integration Tests**:\\n   - Test synchronization with FileWatcher\\n   - Validate incremental update generation\\n   - Check cache consistency\\n   - Error handling during high-frequency changes\\n\\n### FileListAPI Endpoint Tests\\n1. **Unit Tests**:\\n   - Validate GET /api/files/list endpoint\\n   - Test conditional request handling (304 Not Modified)\\n   - Verify query parameter processing\\n   - Check response payload structure\\n\\n2. **Integration Tests**:\\n   - End-to-end file list retrieval\\n   - Test with various file system states\\n   - Verify authentication and authorization\\n   - Performance and load testing\\n\\n## Frontend Test Tasks\\n\\n### FilePollingService Tests\\n1. **Unit Tests**:\\n   - Validate adaptive polling logic\\n   - Test exponential backoff algorithm\\n   - Verify interval calculations\\n   - Error state management\\n\\n2. **Integration Tests**:\\n   - Polling behavior under different network conditions\\n   - State synchronization\\n   - Error recovery mechanisms\\n\\n### Redux Slice Tests\\n1. **Unit Tests**:\\n   - Test fileListSlice reducers\\n   - Validate state updates\\n   - Check action creator behaviors\\n   - Error state management\\n\\n### React Component Tests\\n1. **Unit Tests**:\\n   - FileListContainer rendering\\n   - FileListDisplay rendering\\n   - Interaction with polling service\\n   - State management\\n\\n2. **Integration Tests**:\\n   - Component interaction\\n   - State propagation\\n   - Rendering with different file list states\\n\\n## End-to-End Test Scenarios\\n1. **File Change Detection**\\n   - Create, modify, delete files\\n   - Verify UI updates\\n   - Check polling interval adaptation\\n\\n2. **Network Resilience**\\n   - Simulate network interruptions\\n   - Test error recovery\\n   - Validate exponential backoff\\n\\n3. **Performance Scenarios**\\n   - Large file system with frequent changes\\n   - Slow network conditions\\n   - High-latency environments\\n\\n## Performance and Load Testing\\n1. File list retrieval under load\\n2. Polling frequency impact\\n3. Memory usage tracking\\n4. Cache efficiency measurement\\n\\n## Security Testing\\n1. Authentication verification\\n2. Authorization checks\\n3. Payload validation\\n4. Rate limiting\\n\\n## Recommended Testing Tools\\n- **Backend**: Jest, Supertest\\n- **Frontend**: React Testing Library, Jest\\n- **E2E**: Playwright\\n- **Performance**: Artillery, k6\\n\\n## Test Environment Configuration\\n- Develop mock file systems\\n- Simulate various network conditions\\n- Create reproducible test scenarios\\n- Implement comprehensive logging\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Polling Overhead**\\n   - Implement adaptive intervals\\n   - Add circuit breakers\\n   - Monitor resource consumption\\n\\n2. **Cache Inconsistency**\\n   - Use checksums for validation\\n   - Implement atomic updates\\n   - Add extensive logging\\n\\n3. **Network Interruptions**\\n   - Design robust retry mechanisms\\n   - Implement graceful degradation\\n   - Provide clear user feedback\\n\\n## Test Execution Strategy\\n1. Run unit tests on every commit\\n2. Integration tests in staging\\n3. E2E tests before release\\n4. Continuous performance monitoring\\n\\n## Reporting and Metrics\\n- Code coverage reports\\n- Performance benchmark results\\n- Error rate tracking\\n- Polling efficiency metrics"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015JiFfsst8SjYDnB11MxLUx', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history