{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 03:07:50", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-44de6c54-312f-4fc7-9a04-b253e24552db', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Achievement System Expansion"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01HF9JXXWQMRS7Pmo6evK7Pd', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01HF9JXXWQMRS7Pmo6evK7Pd', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement System Expansion Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Vision**: Expand the existing achievement system by adding 10 new achievements to every achievement category, enhancing agent engagement and providing more comprehensive recognition for diverse behaviors.\\n\\n## Current State Analysis\\nBased on system analysis, the achievement system currently contains:\\n- **138 total achievements** across 9 categories\\n- **Categories with current counts**:\\n  - ska: 8 achievements\\n  - productivity: 5 achievements \\n  - comedy: 5 achievements\\n  - milestone: 4 achievements\\n  - meta: 4 achievements\\n  - streak: 3 achievements\\n  - brass_band: 15 achievements (already has 10+)\\n  - drum_corps: 15 achievements (already has 10+)\\n  - guitar_hero: 20 achievements (already has 10+)\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Add 10 new achievements to each category** that currently has fewer than 10\\n2. **Maintain thematic consistency** with existing achievement styles\\n3. **Ensure balanced rarity distribution** across new achievements\\n4. **Preserve existing functionality** and database compatibility\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Categories requiring expansion** (add 10 each):\\n  - ska: +10 achievements (current: 8)\\n  - productivity: +10 achievements (current: 5)\\n  - comedy: +10 achievements (current: 5)\\n  - milestone: +10 achievements (current: 4)\\n  - meta: +10 achievements (current: 4)\\n  - streak: +10 achievements (current: 3)\\n\\n- **Categories already meeting requirement** (maintain as-is):\\n  - brass_band: 15 achievements (meets requirement)\\n  - drum_corps: 15 achievements (meets requirement)\\n  - guitar_hero: 20 achievements (meets requirement)\\n\\n### Features to Add\\n- **60 new achievement definitions** total\\n- Appropriate icons, names, descriptions for each\\n- Balanced rarity distribution (common, uncommon, rare, epic, legendary)\\n- Logical trigger conditions that align with agent behaviors\\n- Point values consistent with existing rarity scales\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n- Changing achievement tracking logic or database schema\\n- Altering UI components beyond what\'s necessary for new achievements\\n- Adding new achievement categories\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Code Changes Required\\n- **Primary file**: `/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`\\n- Expand `ACHIEVEMENTS` list with 60 new entries\\n- Follow existing `Achievement` dataclass structure\\n- Maintain thematic naming and icon conventions\\n\\n### Constraints\\n- Must not break existing achievement tracking\\n- New achievements must use existing `AchievementCategory` enum values\\n- Must follow existing rarity point scale:\\n  - Common: 5-15 points\\n  - Uncommon: 15-35 points  \\n  - Rare: 35-60 points\\n  - Epic: 60-100 points\\n  - Legendary: 100-300 points\\n\\n### Quality Standards\\n- All achievements must have unique IDs\\n- Names should be creative and thematically appropriate\\n- Descriptions should be clear and often humorous\\n- Trigger conditions should be implementable with existing tracking\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **60 new achievements added** to specified categories\\n2. **All categories have at least 10 achievements** \\n3. **System maintains backward compatibility**\\n4. **New achievements appear in UI** and can be earned\\n5. **No regression in existing functionality**\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- Existing achievement infrastructure supports additional entries\\n- Current rarity and point distributions should be maintained\\n- Ska music, productivity, comedy, milestone, meta, and streak themes should continue\\n- Agent classes and trigger conditions remain as currently defined\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Achievement tracking system (`AchievementTracker` class)\\n- Achievement database schema\\n- Frontend achievement display components\\n- Agent execution monitoring for trigger detection\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Updated `achievements.py` with 60 new achievement definitions\\n- Verification that all categories meet the 10-achievement minimum\\n- Testing to ensure new achievements integrate properly with existing system"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016j1R51oLLQNSXxREBWLeru', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Achievement System Expansion - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project**: Achievement System Expansion  \n**Goal**: Add 10 new achievements to each category with fewer than 10 achievements (60 total new achievements)  \n**Duration**: Estimated 1-2 development cycles  \n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Achievement Design and Implementation\n**Timeline**: 1 development cycle  \n**Lead**: Backend focus with testing coordination  \n\n#### Objective\nDesign and implement all 60 new achievements across the 6 target categories, ensuring thematic consistency and balanced rarity distribution.\n\n#### Deliverables\n- 60 new achievement definitions in `achievements.py`\n- Proper categorization and rarity distribution\n- Thematically appropriate names, descriptions, and icons\n- Point values following existing scales\n\n#### Tasks\n- **Backend Development**:\n  - Analyze existing achievement patterns per category\n  - Design 10 new achievements for each target category:\n    - ska: +10 achievements (current: 8) \n    - productivity: +10 achievements (current: 5)\n    - comedy: +10 achievements (current: 5) \n    - milestone: +10 achievements (current: 4)\n    - meta: +10 achievements (current: 4)\n    - streak: +10 achievements (current: 3)\n  - Implement achievement definitions following existing `Achievement` dataclass structure\n  - Ensure unique IDs and proper categorization\n  - Validate rarity distribution and point values\n\n- **Testing**:\n  - Unit tests for new achievement definitions\n  - Integration tests with existing achievement system\n  - Validation that new achievements can be triggered\n  - Regression tests for existing achievements\n\n#### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ All 60 new achievements added to `achievements.py`\n- ✅ Each target category has exactly 10 additional achievements\n- ✅ Rarity distribution follows existing patterns\n- ✅ All achievement names are unique and thematically consistent\n- ✅ Point values align with rarity scales (Common: 5-15, Uncommon: 15-35, Rare: 35-60, Epic: 60-100, Legendary: 100-300)\n- ✅ No existing achievements are modified or broken\n- ✅ All tests pass including new and regression tests\n- ✅ Achievement system maintains backward compatibility\n\n#### Dependencies\n- Access to existing `achievements.py` file\n- Understanding of existing achievement tracking infrastructure\n- Knowledge of agent behavior patterns for trigger design\n\n#### Risk Mitigation\n- **Risk**: New achievements may not trigger properly\n  - **Mitigation**: Test trigger conditions against existing agent behavior patterns\n- **Risk**: ID conflicts with existing achievements  \n  - **Mitigation**: Implement systematic ID generation/validation\n- **Risk**: Thematic inconsistency\n  - **Mitigation**: Analyze existing patterns before designing new achievements\n\n### Project Success Metrics\n- **Technical**: All 60 achievements successfully integrated without regression\n- **Quality**: Achievement names and descriptions maintain humor and creativity standards\n- **Functional**: New achievements can be earned and display properly in UI\n- **Compatibility**: Zero impact on existing achievement functionality\n\n### Post-Completion Validation\n1. Verify each target category has at least 10 achievements\n2. Confirm total achievement count increased by exactly 60\n3. Test achievement earning and display functionality\n4. Validate system performance with expanded achievement set\n5. Check that existing achievement earning continues to work\n\nThis single milestone approach ensures rapid delivery while maintaining quality standards. The focused scope allows for thorough testing and validation before completion.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016j1R51oLLQNSXxREBWLeru', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_030619.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_030619.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01M9Ltm2ZPBMqxkuJJ8xqA1M', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Achievement System Expansion'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01M9Ltm2ZPBMqxkuJJ8xqA1M', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Data Extension Pattern architecture designed for minimal-risk achievement system expansion", "key_decisions": ["Data Extension Pattern - Pure additive approach with zero code logic changes", "Maintain existing Python/SQLite tech stack - No technology changes required", "Single-file deployment strategy - Only achievements.py modified", "Follow existing rarity distribution patterns - 60 achievements distributed across Common to Legendary tiers", "Use existing trigger condition patterns - No new condition types needed", "Zero-downtime deployment - New achievements integrate immediately without migration"], "self_analysis": "Successfully analyzed the achievement system expansion requirement and designed an appropriately minimal architecture. Applied the Data Extension Pattern correctly, recognizing this as a pure data addition task requiring no structural changes. The proposal balances technical pragmatism with creative achievement theming while maintaining the robust existing infrastructure."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017SKhC5w1Mm4yxHjLMfFyjg', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017SKhC5w1Mm4yxHjLMfFyjg', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement System Expansion Architecture\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **Data Extension Pattern** implementation - a low-risk architectural approach that expands an existing system\'s data layer without modifying its core structure. The achievement system already has robust infrastructure in place, and our task is to add 60 new achievement definitions to bring underrepresented categories up to a minimum threshold.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Data Extension with Additive Design\\n- No modifications to existing code logic\\n- No database schema changes required\\n- No API alterations needed\\n- Pure additive approach maintains backward compatibility\\n\\n**Rationale**: The existing achievement system is well-architected with proper separation of concerns. The `achievements.py` module cleanly separates achievement definitions from tracking logic. Adding new achievements is simply extending the data layer - the safest possible architectural change.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Current Technology (Maintained)\\n- **Python 3.x** - Core language for the achievement system\\n- **SQLite** - Lightweight database for achievement tracking\\n- **Dataclasses & Enums** - Type-safe achievement definitions\\n- **JSON** - Context serialization for awarded achievements\\n\\n**Why maintain existing stack**: The current implementation is production-ready with proper error handling, database indexing, and logging. No technology changes are needed.\\n\\n### Development Tools (For Implementation)\\n- **Text Editor/IDE** - For code editing\\n- **Python Interpreter** - For syntax validation\\n- **Git** - For version control\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered**: \\n- External achievement service (rejected - adds complexity)\\n- Database migration approach (rejected - unnecessary)\\n- YAML/JSON configuration (rejected - Python dataclasses provide better type safety)\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Existing Components (Unchanged)\\n1. **AchievementTracker Class** - Core tracking logic\\n2. **Database Layer** - SQLite persistence\\n3. **Achievement Definition Schema** - Dataclass structure\\n4. **Condition Checking System** - Trigger evaluation logic\\n5. **Statistics Tracking** - Agent performance metrics\\n\\n### Modified Components\\n1. **ACHIEVEMENTS List** - Will be extended from 138 to 198 total achievements\\n\\n### Data Flow (Unchanged)\\n```\\nAgent Execution \\u2192 AchievementTracker.check_and_award() \\u2192 \\nCondition Evaluation \\u2192 Database Persistence \\u2192 UI Display\\n```\\n\\nThe data flow remains identical. New achievements will seamlessly integrate into existing tracking workflows.\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n### Primary Target File\\n```\\n/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Achievement definitions (ACHIEVEMENTS list) \\u2190 MODIFIED\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementTracker class \\u2190 UNCHANGED\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Database schema \\u2190 UNCHANGED\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Helper methods \\u2190 UNCHANGED\\n```\\n\\n### No New Files Required\\nThe existing architecture is sufficient. All new achievements will be added to the existing `ACHIEVEMENTS` list in `achievements.py`.\\n\\n### Configuration Files (Unchanged)\\n- Database initialization remains automatic\\n- No configuration files need modification\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Existing Achievement Structure (Maintained)\\n```python\\n@dataclass\\nclass Achievement:\\n    id: str                           # Unique identifier\\n    name: str                         # Display name\\n    description: str                  # User-facing description\\n    category: AchievementCategory     # One of 9 categories\\n    rarity: AchievementRarity         # Common to Legendary\\n    icon: str                         # Emoji icon\\n    points: int                       # Point value (5-300)\\n    agent_classes: List[str]          # Eligible agents\\n    trigger_condition: Dict[str, Any] # Activation criteria\\n```\\n\\n### Rarity Distribution Target (New Achievements)\\nFollowing existing patterns:\\n- **Common (5-15 pts)**: ~30% of new achievements (18 achievements)\\n- **Uncommon (15-35 pts)**: ~35% of new achievements (21 achievements)\\n- **Rare (35-60 pts)**: ~25% of new achievements (15 achievements)\\n- **Epic (60-100 pts)**: ~8% of new achievements (5 achievements)\\n- **Legendary (100-300 pts)**: ~2% of new achievements (1 achievement)\\n\\n### Category Expansion Plan\\n```\\nCategories requiring expansion:\\n- ska: 8 \\u2192 18 (+10 achievements)\\n- productivity: 5 \\u2192 15 (+10 achievements) \\n- comedy: 5 \\u2192 15 (+10 achievements)\\n- milestone: 4 \\u2192 14 (+10 achievements)\\n- meta: 4 \\u2192 14 (+10 achievements)\\n- streak: 3 \\u2192 13 (+10 achievements)\\n\\nCategories meeting requirement (unchanged):\\n- brass_band: 15 achievements\\n- drum_corps: 15 achievements  \\n- guitar_hero: 20 achievements\\n```\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n### No API Changes Required\\nThe achievement system uses internal Python APIs that remain unchanged:\\n\\n**Existing Public Interface** (maintained):\\n```python\\n# Primary integration point\\nachievement_tracker.check_and_award(\\n    agent_id: str,\\n    agent_name: str, \\n    agent_class: str,\\n    execution_data: Dict[str, Any]\\n) -> List[AwardedAchievement]\\n\\n# Query methods (unchanged)\\nget_achievements_for_agent(agent_class: str)\\nget_all_achievements() \\nget_recent_achievements(limit: int)\\nget_achievement_stats()\\n```\\n\\n### Trigger Condition Patterns (Extended)\\nNew achievements will use existing trigger condition patterns:\\n- Event-based: `{\\"event\\": \\"event_name\\"}`\\n- Numeric thresholds: `{\\"metric_name\\": {\\"min\\": X, \\"max\\": Y}}`\\n- Time-based: `{\\"time_of_day\\": {\\"start\\": H, \\"end\\": H}}`\\n- Streak-based: `{\\"consecutive_X\\": {\\"min\\": N}}`\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Single-File Deployment\\n**Deployment Method**: Direct file replacement\\n1. Backup current `achievements.py` \\n2. Deploy updated file with 60 new achievements\\n3. Restart application (if necessary)\\n\\n**Zero Downtime**: The existing database and tracking infrastructure can handle new achievements immediately. No migration scripts needed.\\n\\n### Environment Compatibility\\n- **Development**: Direct file edit and test\\n- **Staging**: File replacement with validation\\n- **Production**: File replacement with monitoring\\n\\n### Rollback Strategy\\nSimple file revert to previous version if issues arise. No data loss risk since new achievements only add data, never modify existing records.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Validation Testing\\n```python\\n# 1. Achievement Definition Validation\\ndef test_achievement_definitions():\\n    \\"\\"\\"Ensure all new achievements are valid\\"\\"\\"\\n    - Unique IDs across all 198 achievements\\n    - Valid category/rarity combinations  \\n    - Point values within rarity ranges\\n    - No duplicate names within categories\\n    - Valid emoji icons\\n    - Proper agent class targeting\\n\\n# 2. Count Verification  \\ndef test_category_counts():\\n    \\"\\"\\"Verify each category meets 10+ requirement\\"\\"\\"\\n    for category in [ska, productivity, comedy, milestone, meta, streak]:\\n        assert count >= 10\\n\\n# 3. Integration Testing\\ndef test_achievement_tracking():\\n    \\"\\"\\"Test new achievements integrate properly\\"\\"\\"\\n    - Trigger conditions are evaluable\\n    - Database persistence works\\n    - UI display functions correctly\\n```\\n\\n### Manual Testing\\n1. **Thematic Consistency**: Review achievement names/descriptions for category alignment\\n2. **Rarity Balance**: Verify point distributions match existing patterns\\n3. **Trigger Logic**: Test that conditions can be reasonably achieved\\n4. **UI Integration**: Confirm new achievements display properly\\n\\n### Performance Testing\\n- Load test with 198 achievements vs current 138\\n- Database query performance with expanded dataset\\n- Memory usage validation\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### 1. Database Schema Modification Approach\\n**Rejected**: Would require adding new fields, migration scripts, and API changes. Unnecessarily complex for a data expansion task.\\n\\n### 2. External Configuration File Approach  \\n**Rejected**: Moving achievements to JSON/YAML would lose Python\'s type safety and require parsing logic changes. Current dataclass approach is superior.\\n\\n### 3. Gradual Rollout Approach\\n**Rejected**: Since achievements are additions only with no side effects, phased deployment adds complexity without benefit.\\n\\n### 4. New Achievement Categories\\n**Rejected**: Requirements specify expanding existing categories, not creating new ones. Adding categories would require enum changes and UI modifications.\\n\\n### 5. Achievement Template System\\n**Considered**: Could create templates for similar achievements to reduce code duplication. **Rejected** due to requirements preferring explicit definitions for clarity.\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: ID Collisions\\n**Likelihood**: Low  \\n**Impact**: High (database conflicts)  \\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive ID uniqueness validation before deployment\\n\\n### Risk 2: Thematic Inconsistency  \\n**Likelihood**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: Low (user experience degradation)  \\n**Mitigation**: Thorough review of achievement names/descriptions against existing patterns\\n\\n### Risk 3: Trigger Condition Bugs\\n**Likelihood**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: Medium (achievements not triggering)  \\n**Mitigation**: Test trigger conditions against existing execution data patterns\\n\\n### Risk 4: Performance Impact\\n**Likelihood**: Low  \\n**Impact**: Medium (slower achievement checking)  \\n**Mitigation**: Load testing with 60 additional achievements, database indexing review\\n\\n### Risk 5: Point Economy Inflation\\n**Likelihood**: Low  \\n**Impact**: Low (achievement value perception)  \\n**Mitigation**: Follow existing rarity/point distributions precisely\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### User Input Needed\\n1. **Thematic Direction**: For achievements requiring creative naming, should we emphasize humor, technical accuracy, or music references?\\n\\n2. **Trigger Complexity**: Should new achievements use only existing trigger patterns, or can we introduce new condition types (like agent collaboration events)?\\n\\n3. **Rarity Distribution**: The proposed distribution follows existing patterns. Should any categories emphasize higher/lower rarity achievements?\\n\\n4. **Agent Class Targeting**: Should new achievements target specific agent classes more precisely, or maintain the current broad targeting approach?\\n\\n### Technical Decisions (Recommended Defaults)\\n- **Icon Selection**: Use standard emoji set for consistency \\u2713\\n- **Naming Convention**: Follow existing patterns (puns, references, technical terms) \\u2713\\n- **Description Style**: Maintain humorous tone with technical accuracy \\u2713\\n- **Point Values**: Strict adherence to existing rarity scales \\u2713\\n\\n## Implementation Timeline\\n\\n### Phase 1: Preparation (1 hour)\\n- Analyze existing achievement patterns per category\\n- Create achievement templates following existing themes\\n- Validate ID uniqueness strategy\\n\\n### Phase 2: Creation (3-4 hours)  \\n- Design 60 new achievements with proper distribution\\n- Implement trigger conditions using existing patterns\\n- Validate all definitions for consistency\\n\\n### Phase 3: Integration (1 hour)\\n- Add achievements to ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n- Run validation tests\\n- Verify database compatibility\\n\\n### Phase 4: Testing (1 hour)\\n- Test trigger condition logic\\n- Validate UI integration  \\n- Performance testing with expanded dataset\\n\\n**Total Estimated Time**: 6-7 hours\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Quantitative Goals**:\\n   - 60 new achievements successfully added\\n   - All 6 target categories have \\u226510 achievements\\n   - Zero breaking changes to existing functionality\\n   - Database performance impact <5%\\n\\n2. **Qualitative Goals**:\\n   - New achievements maintain thematic consistency\\n   - Trigger conditions are achievable but appropriately challenging\\n   - Rarity distribution matches existing patterns\\n   - User experience remains seamless\\n\\nThis architecture provides a minimal-risk path to meeting the expansion requirements while maintaining the robust foundation of the existing achievement system."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create'