{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 03:08:04", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f5c3e4ee-5fee-4865-aa9e-e2fb3013a882', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/dnd_achievements_requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "D&D Achievements Addition"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XmyBkCKDk2MW1HdLkv6BhK', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/dnd_achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XmyBkCKDk2MW1HdLkv6BhK', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# D&D Achievements Addition - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** D&D Achievements Addition  \\n**Project ID:** 39ccaa61  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-15  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nAdd 10 new achievements from the \\"Dungeons and Dragons\\" category to the existing achievements system. These achievements should capture the essence of D&D gameplay, character creation, storytelling, and adventure mechanics while maintaining the humorous, tongue-in-cheek tone of the existing achievement system.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Define D&D Achievement Category**: Add `DUNGEONS_DRAGONS = \\"dungeons_dragons\\"` to the existing `AchievementCategory` enum\\n2. **Create 10 D&D Achievements**: Design achievements that reference:\\n   - Character classes (Fighter, Wizard, Rogue, Cleric, etc.)\\n   - Dice rolling mechanics (Natural 20s, Critical fails)\\n   - Campaign elements (Dungeons, Dragons, NPCs, Quests)\\n   - Player behaviors (Min-maxing, Roleplay, Rules lawyering)\\n   - Classic D&D tropes and memes\\n\\n3. **Integration**: Add achievements to the existing `ACHIEVEMENTS` list in the achievements system\\n4. **Preserve Existing Functionality**: Ensure new achievements work with existing tracking and display systems\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Achievement Definitions:**\\n- 10 new achievements with D&D themes\\n- Appropriate trigger conditions that can be detected from agent behavior\\n- Mix of rarity levels (Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, Legendary)\\n- Humorous descriptions that reference D&D culture\\n- Appropriate emoji icons\\n- Point values consistent with existing achievements\\n\\n**D&D Achievement Examples:**\\n- \\"Natural 20\\" - Perfect execution on first try\\n- \\"Critical Fumble\\" - Spectacular failure that leads to comedy\\n- \\"Rules Lawyer\\" - Agent that\'s overly pedantic about specifications\\n- \\"Dungeon Master\\" - Agent that spawns and manages many sub-agents\\n- \\"Min-Maxer\\" - Agent that optimizes for efficiency metrics\\n- \\"Charisma Build\\" - Agent with particularly engaging output\\n- \\"TPK (Total Party Kill)\\" - All spawned agents fail simultaneously\\n- \\"Dragon Slayer\\" - Agent that tackles the biggest, most complex tasks\\n- \\"Tavern Keeper\\" - Agent that provides support/coordination for others\\n- \\"Loot Goblin\\" - Agent that generates many files/artifacts\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- New UI components (achievements system already has display mechanisms)\\n- New tracking mechanisms (existing system handles all needed events)\\n- Changes to database schema (existing tables support new achievements)\\n- New API endpoints (existing achievement APIs will serve new achievements)\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Achievement Data Structure\\nEach new achievement must follow the existing `Achievement` dataclass format:\\n```python\\nAchievement(\\n    id=\\"unique_snake_case_id\\",\\n    name=\\"Display Name\\",\\n    description=\\"Humorous description with D&D flavor\\",\\n    category=AchievementCategory.DUNGEONS_DRAGONS,\\n    rarity=AchievementRarity.COMMON,  # or UNCOMMON, RARE, EPIC, LEGENDARY\\n    icon=\\"\\ud83c\\udfb2\\",  # Appropriate emoji\\n    points=25,  # Points consistent with rarity\\n    agent_classes=[\\"*\\"],  # Which agents can earn it\\n    trigger_condition={\\"event\\": \\"condition_name\\"}  # Detectable condition\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Trigger Conditions\\nMust use existing trigger condition patterns that can be detected from agent execution data:\\n- Event-based: `{\\"event\\": \\"event_name\\"}`\\n- Numeric thresholds: `{\\"metric_name\\": {\\"min\\": value}}`\\n- Duration-based: `{\\"duration_ms\\": {\\"min\\": value, \\"max\\": value}}`\\n- Success/failure patterns: `{\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": value}}`\\n\\n### Category Addition\\nAdd to `AchievementCategory` enum:\\n```python\\nDUNGEONS_DRAGONS = \\"dungeons_dragons\\"  # D&D themed achievements\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional:**\\n   - \\u2705 10 new D&D achievements defined and integrated\\n   - \\u2705 New achievements appear in achievement gallery\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements can be earned based on trigger conditions\\n   - \\u2705 All existing achievement functionality remains intact\\n\\n2. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements reference authentic D&D concepts and terminology\\n   - \\u2705 Descriptions are humorous and engaging\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions are realistic and achievable through normal agent behavior\\n   - \\u2705 Point values and rarity levels are balanced with existing achievements\\n\\n3. **Technical:**\\n   - \\u2705 Code follows existing patterns and conventions\\n   - \\u2705 New achievements integrate seamlessly with existing system\\n   - \\u2705 No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n\\n## D&D Achievement Concepts\\n\\n### Character Classes\\n- **Fighter** - Straightforward, reliable task completion\\n- **Wizard** - Complex problem-solving with many steps\\n- **Rogue** - Finding clever workarounds or shortcuts\\n- **Cleric** - Supporting/healing other agents\' failures\\n- **Barbarian** - Brute-force approaches that work despite being inelegant\\n- **Bard** - Particularly creative or eloquent output\\n\\n### Dice Mechanics\\n- **Natural 20** - Perfect success on first attempt\\n- **Natural 1** - Spectacular failure\\n- **Advantage** - Multiple approaches tried, best one succeeds\\n- **Disadvantage** - Success despite obstacles\\n\\n### Campaign Elements\\n- **Dungeon Crawl** - Navigating complex nested structures\\n- **Dragon Encounter** - Tackling the biggest, scariest tasks\\n- **NPC Interaction** - Working with external systems/APIs\\n- **Treasure Hoard** - Generating valuable outputs/artifacts\\n\\n### Player Behaviors\\n- **Min-Maxing** - Optimizing for specific metrics\\n- **Rules Lawyer** - Being overly pedantic about requirements\\n- **Murder Hobo** - Aggressive approach that destroys obstacles\\n- **Pacifist** - Solving problems without \\"violence\\" (errors/failures)\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Existing System**: The achievements system is already implemented and functional\\n2. **Integration Point**: New achievements will be added to the `ACHIEVEMENTS` list in `achievements.py`\\n3. **Trigger Detection**: Existing agent execution tracking provides sufficient data to detect D&D achievement conditions\\n4. **UI Support**: Achievement gallery and notification systems already support category-based filtering\\n5. **User Interest**: Users will appreciate D&D-themed humor and references\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n1. **Maintainability**: Follow existing code patterns and conventions\\n2. **Performance**: New achievements should not impact system performance\\n3. **Accessibility**: D&D references should be understandable to general developer audience\\n4. **Localization**: English-only initially (consistent with existing achievements)\\n\\n## Risks & Mitigations\\n\\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\\n|------|--------|------------|\\n| D&D references too niche/obscure | Medium | Use widely known D&D concepts and tropes |\\n| Trigger conditions not achievable | Medium | Base conditions on observable agent behaviors |\\n| Inconsistent with existing tone | Low | Follow humor and style patterns of existing achievements |\\n| Integration breaks existing system | High | Thorough testing and code review |\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n1. **Requirements Complete** \\u2705\\n2. **Add D&D Category** - Add enum value to `AchievementCategory`\\n3. **Define 10 Achievements** - Create achievement definitions with appropriate:\\n   - Names and descriptions\\n   - Trigger conditions\\n   - Rarity and point values\\n   - Agent class restrictions\\n4. **Integration** - Add achievements to `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\\n5. **Testing** - Verify achievements can be earned and display correctly\\n6. **Documentation** - Update any relevant docs\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Development Manager  \\n**Next Step:** Spawn Development Manager to implement the D&D achievements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ShS6CCj5a4AxZGst22hFdy', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# D&D Achievements Addition - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project:** D&D Achievements Addition  \n**Objective:** Add 10 new Dungeons & Dragons themed achievements to existing system  \n**Duration:** Single milestone implementation (estimated 1-2 development cycles)\n\n## Milestone 1: D&D Achievements Implementation\n**Objective:** Complete integration of 10 D&D themed achievements into existing system\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. **Category Enhancement**\n   - Add `DUNGEONS_DRAGONS = "dungeons_dragons"` to `AchievementCategory` enum\n   \n2. **Achievement Definitions**\n   - 10 new D&D achievements with appropriate:\n     - Names referencing D&D concepts (classes, dice, campaign elements)\n     - Humorous descriptions maintaining existing system tone\n     - Realistic trigger conditions based on agent behaviors\n     - Balanced rarity levels and point values\n     - Appropriate emoji icons\n   \n3. **System Integration**\n   - Add achievements to existing `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\n   - Ensure compatibility with existing tracking/display systems\n   \n4. **Testing & Verification**\n   - Verify achievements can be earned\n   - Confirm display in achievement gallery\n   - Ensure no breaking changes to existing functionality\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- ✅ 10 D&D achievements defined and integrated\n- ✅ New category appears in achievement system\n- ✅ Achievements can be triggered by realistic agent behaviors\n- ✅ Point values and rarity consistent with existing achievements\n- ✅ All existing achievement functionality preserved\n- ✅ D&D references authentic and humorous\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Existing achievements system (already implemented)\n- Agent execution tracking system (provides trigger data)\n- Achievement display components (already functional)\n\n### Technical Requirements:\n- Follow existing `Achievement` dataclass structure\n- Use detectable trigger conditions from current system\n- Maintain code patterns and conventions\n- No database schema changes required\n- No new API endpoints needed\n\n### Risk Mitigation:\n- Use widely known D&D concepts to ensure broad appeal\n- Base trigger conditions on observable agent behaviors\n- Follow existing achievement humor and style patterns\n- Thorough testing to prevent system integration issues\n\n## Success Metrics:\n- All 10 achievements successfully integrated\n- No performance degradation\n- Positive user reception of D&D themes\n- Seamless integration with existing achievement workflows\n\n## Timeline:\nSingle milestone - estimated completion within 1-2 development iterations\n\n---\n**Status:** Planning Complete - Ready for Architecture Phase'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ShS6CCj5a4AxZGst22hFdy', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_030642.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_030642.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Mx4biRcu9ZRXzLo2PSAYiW', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/dnd_achievements_requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'D&D Achievements Addition'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Mx4biRcu9ZRXzLo2PSAYiW', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Jx6vjcSeKzrtG5kS2GMQTn', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/dnd_achievements_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'D&D Achievements Addition'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Jx6vjcSeKzrtG5kS2GMQTn', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Data extension architecture using Additive Pattern for low-risk D&D achievement integration. Single-file modification approach with zero deployment risk and full backward compatibility.", "key_decisions": ["Additive Pattern over separate service - minimizes risk while maximizing code reuse", "Single file modification (achievements.py) - reduces integration complexity and testing surface", "Generic trigger conditions using existing patterns - ensures reliability over D&D-specific detection", "Code-based configuration following existing patterns - maintains type safety and consistency", "Balanced rarity distribution (4 Common, 3 Uncommon, 2 Rare, 1 Epic) - accessibility with prestigious rewards"], "self_analysis": "Successfully analyzed a content addition requirement and designed an appropriately minimal architecture using the Data Extension Pattern. The proposal balances D&D authenticity with technical pragmatism, provides comprehensive risk analysis, and maintains the established low-risk approach for additive changes to stable systems."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
